* VALID_OS_NAME(name)
* Return @true if name is a safe Linux user/group identifier for OS.EXECUTE.
* Copyright (c) String Database
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    x = !valid_os_name(name)
*
*    Validates non-empty name, length <= MAX.USERNAME.LEN, and character set
*    (no shell metacharacters).
*
* 18 Aug 26 Windows port - this used to say the character set was "aligned with
*   SETSRVR user.name.chars".  SETSRVR went with SDNet on 18 Aug 2026, so the
*   comparison named a program that no longer exists.  The rule is stated here
*   instead of pointing at another file for it.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function valid_os_name(name)
$catalog !valid_os_name

$include int$keys.h

   * Modified by Composer AI - 2026/06/10.
   * Shared validation for OS.EXECUTE name arguments (phase 2).
   os.name.chars = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-'
   if name = '' then return @false
   if len(name) > MAX.USERNAME.LEN then return @false
   if convert(os.name.chars, '', name) # '' then return @false
   * --------------------
   return @true

end

* END-CODE
